    moveValidityConditions: {
      take_stock: 'Current active player only; at most one take this turn; stock must not be empty.',
      take_discard: 'Current active player only; at most one take this turn; discard pile must not be empty.',
      discard_card: 'Current active player only; at most one discard this turn; player must keep at least three cards.',
      declare_suit: 'Current active player only; player must hold at least one card of the suit and must not already be declared.',
      end_turn: 'Current active player only; applies undeclared debt only if the player acted this turn and is still undeclared.',
      timeout_turn: 'No-action timeout advances safely; timeout after an action resolves like an undeclared end turn.',
      call_showdown: 'Current active declared player only; final score must be at least 27 with at least three cards in hand.',
    },
    LLM: 'Claim is a four-player suit-collection card game. Each round deals three cards to every active player from a standard 52-card French deck. Players privately declare one suit, collect cards of that suit, and avoid holding other suits. On a turn, a player may take once from stock or discard, discard once, declare, and end the turn. Ending an acted turn while undeclared adds persistent debt equal to the highest card in hand. Showdown reveals all hands and scores declared-suit runs as positive, off-suit or undeclared runs as negative, then subtracts debt. Raw scores affect bankrolls and a positive top score also earns winner-difference payouts.',
    Player: 'Collect one suit, secretly declare it, and build enough score to call Showdown. You start each round with three cards. You may take from stock or discard, discard a card while keeping at least three cards, or end your turn. If you act and stay undeclared, you add debt. Showdown needs a declared suit, at least three cards, and final score 27 or higher.',
  },
}
